> **Key Messages for Ministries of Finance:**
> 
> - **Integrate Climate Risks into Planning:** Finance Ministries should incorporate climate risks and adaptation investments into macroeconomic projections and capital planning to address rising fiscal demands from climate change.
> 
> - **Build Analytical Capabilities:** Invest in analytical tools and skills to assess climate risks and opportunities. Utilize a diverse range of models beyond traditional approaches, considering factors like tipping points and non-marginal changes.
> 
> - **Develop a Long-Term Vision:** Collaborate with other government departments to set clear goals for climate resilience and envision a well-adapted economy, informed by thorough analysis of current and future risks and costs.
> 
> - **Strategic Integration and Enabling Conditions:** Support strategic integration of adaptation into national plans and expenditure frameworks, and create enabling conditions through policy reforms. Prioritize "no regret" options and infrastructure with long-term benefits.
> 
> - **Collaborative National Adaptation Plans:** Play a pivotal role in developing national adaptation strategies, aligning them with budget processes, and addressing contingent liabilities from physical risks. Consider stress-testing financial institutions and incorporating disaster clauses in debt strategies.
